      "agent_id": "WebSearch",
      "message": "{\n  \"summary\": \"The official Python documentation on decorators, such as PEP 318, describes decorators as a way to transform functions and methods, often used to add functionality or modify behavior without changing the original code. It emphasizes the technical aspects and syntax, including the use of the '@' symbol and higher-order functions. In contrast, Real Python provides a more conceptual and tutorial-oriented explanation, highlighting that decorators allow modification or extension of function behavior without altering the function's code directly. It explains decorators as functions that wrap other functions, enabling code reuse and cleaner syntax, and offers practical guidance on creating and using decorators. Overall, the official docs focus on formal definitions and specifications, while Real Python offers accessible, example-driven explanations suitable for learners.\",\n  \"sources\": [\n    \"https://peps.python.org/pep-0318/\",\n    \"https://realpython.com/primer-on-python-decorators/\"\n  ]\n}",
